#: src/algorithm_settings.c:66
msgid ""
"Sets the cutoff for both the raw-audio high-pass and the tick-envelope low-"
"pass. Raising it rejects more low-frequency vibration but preserves finer "
"detail in the envelope."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:67
msgid ""
"Mutes audio where the windowed energy exceeds this multiple of the reference "
"level. Higher values mute less; use a higher value if strong, genuine ticks "
"are being removed. Full mode only."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:68
msgid ""
"Sets how much audio is combined into each local energy measurement. A longer "
"window spreads the influence of a short impact over more time. Full mode "
"only."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:69
msgid ""
"Takes the highest local energy in each segment, then uses the median of "
"those peaks as the reference. Longer segments mean fewer reference "
"measurements per analysis block. Full mode only."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:70
msgid ""
"With manual BPH, searches this far on either side of the expected tic-to-tic "
"interval. Widen it if a clock gains or loses enough to put the true period "
"outside the window. This setting also affects automatic BPH checks."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:71
msgid ""
"After finding the initial period, searches this far around each predicted "
"correlation peak. Widen only if the correct peak falls outside the window; a "
"wider search can pick a neighboring peak."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:72
msgid ""
"A shorter candidate period must exceed this percentage of the original "
"correlation peak to be accepted. Higher values make Auto less willing to "
"choose the shorter period."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:73
msgid ""
"Compares the correlation near 1.5 times the candidate period with the peak "
"at the candidate period. A value below this threshold triggers a check for a "
"doubled period. Raising the threshold makes that check more likely."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:74
msgid ""
"Looks for the opposite beat near halfway through the measured cycle. Widen "
"it if tic and toc are genuinely uneven; a steady gain or loss is not a "
"reason to widen it."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:75
msgid ""
"Smooths the combined tic/toc envelope before choosing its timing reference. "
"More smoothing reduces fine detail but can shift the point used for "
"alignment."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:76
msgid ""
"When combining repeated cycles into one waveform, discards the highest "
"values at each phase position before averaging. Higher values reject more "
"isolated spikes, but unusual loud beats contribute less to the result."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:77
msgid ""
"Searches this far around each predicted tick for a trace dot. A wider window "
"may recover missing dots or pick another peak from the same tick. It does "
"not widen the initial rate search."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:78
msgid ""
"Smooths the waveform before looking for lift pulses. More smoothing can "
"reduce ripples but can also merge nearby acoustic features."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:79
msgid ""
"Sets the starting signal threshold relative to the strongest point in the "
"smoothed waveform. The background-based threshold takes precedence if it is "
"higher."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:80
msgid ""
"Sets a threshold from the estimated background level. Raising it makes weak "
"features less likely to be accepted as lift pulses."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:81
msgid ""
"Stops the search when the trial signal threshold reaches this percentage of "
"the waveform peak. Raising it allows the detector to try higher thresholds; "
"it does not raise the maximum balance amplitude."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:82
msgid ""
"Rejects a result if either the tic or toc amplitude estimate does not exceed "
"this value. Lowering it can admit a weaker swing, but it does not improve "
"pulse detection."
msgstr ""

#: src/algorithm_settings.c:83
msgid ""
"Accepts a pulse pair only if the two inferred amplitudes differ by less than "
"this value. Raising it permits more disagreement; it does not make the "
"estimates more accurate."
msgstr ""

